    "belle_faq_pricing": {
      "type": "belle-faq-section",
      "blocks": {
        "question_how_it_works": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does drop-off and pickup work?",
            "answer": "<p>When you book, you choose a convenient Northland meetup spot from a list of Kansas City Northland QuikTrip locations. I meet you at your scheduled time, confirm your racquet details, and take it for stringing. Once it's done, I contact you to arrange pickup, usually at the same place you dropped it off.</p>",
            "category": ""
          }
        },
        "question_service_area": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you meet outside the Kansas City Northland?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, within limits. Belle's serves the Kansas City Northland, and drop-off and pickup happen at a QuikTrip in that area at your scheduled time.</p><p>If you're outside the Northland:</p><ul><li>Meeting at one of my Northland QuikTrip locations is the default. Traveling to you is the exception, not the default.</li><li>Ask before you book. It isn't guaranteed and depends on my schedule and route that day.</li><li>I won't travel more than 20 miles from the 9600 N Oak QuikTrip.</li><li>Turnaround may shift. Standard, express, and rush windows are built around the Northland meetup pattern, so an out-of-area meetup may mean a slower turnaround.</li><li>If a request can't be accommodated, I'll tell you before the racquet changes hands.</li></ul>",
            "category": ""
          }
        },
        "question_how_to_pay": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I pay?",
            "answer": "<p>When your racquet is ready, I send you an invoice you can pay online. I accept all major credit cards. No deposits required.</p>",
            "category": ""
          }
        },
        "question_turnaround": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does stringing take?",
            "answer": "<p>Most racquets are ready within 2-3 days. That covers the drop-off meet, a stringing slot in the week, and the return trip.</p><p>Same-day service is available when I pick up your racquet before 10 am. You get it back by 6 pm that evening at the meeting location.</p><p>If I pick up after 10 am, next day is the fastest option. Rush and express pricing is in the table above.</p><p>Go ahead and book. Same-day depends on my schedule, my travel that day, the condition of the racquet, and string availability if you're using mine. I'll confirm same-day is a go, or tell you the fastest real option, before I take the racquet.</p><p>You're welcome to borrow a free Solinco demo racquet while yours is being strung.</p>",
            "category": ""
          }
        },
        "question_string_choice": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need to know what string I want?",
            "answer": "<p>No. If you liked how your racquet played before, I can match your existing setup. If you want to change strings or aren't sure, I can help you choose based on your racquet, playing level, and goals.</p>",
            "category": ""
          }
        },
        "question_out_of_stock": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if you don't carry the string I want?",
            "answer": "<p>Go ahead and book. I stock Solinco, Gosen, Wilson, and Head, and once you're on the calendar, tell me what string you're using or want. I'll confirm before I take your racquet: whether I have it in stock, need to order it (adds a few days), or should suggest something close and why. If you'd rather not wait on an order, you can always bring your own string and pay the customer-supplied rate.</p>",
            "category": ""
          }
        },
        "question_byo": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I bring my own string?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. If you have a string you prefer that I don't carry, bring it and I'll string it. Customer-supplied labor rates are in the table above.</p><p>Tell me what string it is when you book. Natural gut and other delicate strings need special handling, and I'll tell you before I take the racquet if a rush window isn't right for it. Replacement of customer-supplied string damaged during installation is not guaranteed.</p>",
            "category": ""
          }
        },
        "question_diy_machine": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Should I buy a stringing machine so I can string my own racquet?",
            "answer": "<p>If you play tennis for a living and travel most weeks, maybe. Entry-level drop-weight machines start around $150, but a machine that pulls tension the way mine does, electronic constant-pull, starts north of $2,000, plus a mount, clamps, and a real time investment to learn.</p><p>If you're a recreational or high school player restringing every few weeks, the math doesn't work. String twice a month with Belle's and you're paying around $1,300 a year. A $2,000+ constant-pull machine doesn't pay for itself at that pace, and a $150 machine won't give you a better string bed than dead strings did. It pays for itself for someone stringing dozens of racquets a year, not a handful.</p><p>There's also the learning curve. My first racquet took over four hours. The knots were ugly. I made a mess of it. Getting to a consistent, accurate string bed takes real practice, and a bad string job can hurt your play more than dead strings ever would.</p><p>If you're stringing a few times a year, a machine is a bigger investment than the problem calls for. That's what I'm here for.</p>",
            "category": ""
          }
        }
      },
